<http://data.silknow.org/event/33feecca-52f1-3504-ac2d-92eef6528765>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Registered File number 1992/524.\n\nMary Groome is the daughter of John (a linen weaver) and Mary Groome. She was baptised on November the 13 1687 at Ipswich, St. Stephen. She married Matthew Wealy, an ironmonger, also of Ipswich, on May 15 1711. She was buried on July 27 1721.  All these details are from Suffolk Record Office FB 107/D1/2 (Ipswich St Stephens records).\nHer husband's will = CPC/53 Auber /feb 19 1729-30.  \nMary Groome was a pupil of Judith Hayle."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/55fe902a-ceed-3c43-aea0-2ab56d80390d> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Margaret Simeon" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/3c6fefb0-798f-308b-890d-d32014ab5d79> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Registered File number 1992/524.\n\nMary Groome is the daughter of John (a linen weaver) and Mary Groome. She was baptised on November the 13 1687 at Ipswich, St. Stephen. She married Matthew Wealy, an ironmonger, also of Ipswich, on May 15 1711. She was buried on July 27 1721.  All these details are from Suffolk Record Office FB 107/D1/2 (Ipswich St Stephens records).\nHer husband's will = CPC/53 Auber /feb 19 1729-30.  \nMary Groome was a pupil of Judith Hayle."@en .

